w the words I listen in the car I  read a bit of us email all of those  things once I got the book you know I  can do as much of it as I want and so I  don't have to deliberately arranged a  meeting with a tutor however in the case  of Farsi I am finding it great  especially since we don't have  text-to-speech and I simply don't know  how some words are pronounced I find it  very good to have that session with with  Rana in Farsi so I think one important  rule in language learning is variate mix  it up don't get too stuck in dogmatic  positions and try to enjoy it and  usually with enough time and and  exposure you will eventually reach your  goals bye for now  [Music]
 

